WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.501
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:14.415
Unit ten: Books and Reading. In this unit, you will talk about what you are reading now.

4
00:00:15.417 --> 00:00:16.290
Novel.

5
00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.268
Novel means a long story in a book.

6
00:00:19.568 --> 00:00:21.266
I'm reading an adventure novel.

7
00:00:21.966 --> 00:00:24.665
Your turn. Say: Novel.

8
00:00:27.365 --> 00:00:28.192
Novel.

9
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:30.010
Author.

10
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.896
Author means the person who writes a book.

11
00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:34.766
Who is the author of this book?

12
00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:37.526
Your turn. Say: Author.

13
00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:41.018
Author.

14
00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:42.774
Chapter.

15
00:00:43.474 --> 00:00:45.891
Chapter means one part of a book.

16
00:00:46.191 --> 00:00:48.017
I read one chapter every night.

17
00:00:48.717 --> 00:00:51.149
Your turn. Say: Chapter.

18
00:00:53.849 --> 00:00:54.734
Chapter.

19
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.681
Character.

20
00:00:57.381 --> 00:00:59.416
Character means a person in a story.

21
00:00:59.716 --> 00:01:01.727
The main character is very brave.

22
00:01:02.427 --> 00:01:05.300
Your turn. Say: Character.

23
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:08.920
Character.

24
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:10.686
Story.

25
00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:15.069
Story means a description of events, real or imagined.

26
00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:17.206
Grandpa tells great stories.

27
00:01:17.906 --> 00:01:20.535
Your turn. Say: Story.

28
00:01:23.235 --> 00:01:24.178
Story.

29
00:01:25.183 --> 00:01:26.219
Library.

30
00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:29.441
Library means a place where you can borrow books.

31
00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:31.903
I borrowed this book from the library.

32
00:01:32.603 --> 00:01:34.965
Your turn. Say: Library.

33
00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:38.574
Library.

34
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:40.457
Recommend.

35
00:01:41.157 --> 00:01:43.841
Recommend means to tell others that something is good.

36
00:01:44.141 --> 00:01:45.804
Can you recommend a good book?

37
00:01:46.504 --> 00:01:48.901
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

38
00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:52.649
Recommend.

39
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:54.802
Imagination.

40
00:01:55.502 --> 00:01:58.767
Imagination means the ability to make pictures in your mind.

41
00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.299
Reading helps my imagination grow.

42
00:02:01.999 --> 00:02:04.930
Your turn. Say: Imagination.

43
00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:08.805
Imagination.

44
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:11.816
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:12.116 --> 00:02:14.174
Sreypich, what are you reading at the moment?

46
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:17.494
I'm reading a novel about a brave girl.

47
00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:19.866
Who is the author?

48
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.569
A Cambodian author. She writes exciting chapters!

49
00:02:25.883 --> 00:02:27.384
What is your sister reading?

50
00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:30.787
She's reading a comic from the library.

51
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:35.453
Grammar focus: Present continuous (I'm reading ).

52
00:02:35.753 --> 00:02:38.475
I'm reading a novel. She's reading a comic.

53
00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:42.609
Use the present continuous for actions happening now or around now.

54
00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:46.246
Now read and listen. A Book I Love.

55
00:02:46.546 --> 00:02:49.637
I'm reading a novel about a brave girl who saves her village.

56
00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:54.261
The author writes exciting chapters, and I can't stop reading.

57
00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.268
The main character never gives up, even when things are difficult.

58
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:02.792
I borrowed the book from the school library.

59
00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:07.824
Reading helps my imagination grow, and I recommend it to everyone.

60
00:03:09.117 --> 00:03:11.641
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:13.813
I blank reading a novel now.

62
00:03:14.113 --> 00:03:16.745
A, am. B, is. C, are.

63
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.204
The answer is A: am.

64
00:03:23.717 --> 00:03:25.856
The person who writes a book is the blank.

65
00:03:26.156 --> 00:03:29.623
A, author. B, character. C, chapter.

66
00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:35.570
The answer is A: author.

67
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.769
One part of a book is a blank.

68
00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:43.269
A, chapter. B, library. C, novel.

69
00:03:47.283 --> 00:03:49.596
The answer is A: chapter.

70
00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:54.490
Now it's your turn to speak. Who is your favourite book character?

71
00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:05.426
My favourite character is Harry Potter because he is brave and loyal. I'm reading the third book now.

72
00:04:05.726 --> 00:04:07.517
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:08.517 --> 00:04:13.050
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present continuous (i'm reading ).

74
00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:17.361
Today's value is love of reading. Read a book every day.

75
00:04:17.661 --> 00:04:20.104
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

76
00:04:20.404 --> 00:04:23.196
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

